{
    "name": "ghostty-terminal",
    "title": "Ghostty",
    "description": "Ghostty: a real terminal in Pi Pocket, in panes beside a session. The shell runs on the server in the session's folder, and Ghostty's own engine (libghostty-vt) draws its screen, so an editor's cursor shapes, its icons, and its clipboard work as they do in Ghostty. It needs Bun, and a one-time install of libghostty-vt in its runtime folder, ~/.pi-pocket/ghostty-terminal.",
    "tags": [
        "terminal",
        "shell",
        "pty",
        "ghostty",
        "neovim",
        "editor"
    ],
